      en: ["Part of the Portobelo-San Lorenzo UNESCO World Heritage site.", "Constructed using local stone and high-quality masonry.", "Strategically paired with Fort San Fernando across the bay.", "Built to withstand heavy naval bombardments.", "Ruins include well-preserved gun platforms and sentry boxes.", "Located in a rugged and scenic coastal environment.", "Essential for understanding the evolution of Portobelo's defenses.", "A key site for maritime archaeology enthusiasts."],
